{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta","id":1133131,"title":"Why do you like WtA?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-23T13:10:45-07:00","id":1133131,"title":"Why do you like WtA?","content":"There are such topics in Exalted section, so I want to start this one. I'm actually DON'T like Garou. On the hater level. But... I would like to ead about why people can root to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T19:55:05-07:00","id":1134719,"title":"","content":"Personally, I love the spiritual nature of the Garou. As a person, I love being in nature, and seeing the beauty of the Earth. Having a setting where the Earth is literally alive, and your purpose is to protect that speaks to me. The fact that it's also mixed with a horror setting, which happens to be my favorite genre just doubles up on two things that I've always appreciated.<br /> <br /> I also feel like Werewolf allows for a large variety of subject matter for storylines. You can have internal or external Sept politics. You can have the body horror/slash em up style of gameplay. You can have characters caught between their dual natures of having once been human (If you're a Homid born) and you're new life as a monster, dealing with the Rage burning inside of you. You can have adventures into the Near Realms or Deep Umbra that can hit on nearly any topic you want. And while other game settings can have these types of stories as well, I feel like the game gives you near endless possibilities while keeping a unique theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T03:24:54-07:00","id":1134794,"title":"","content":"Spiritualism, Political incorrectness, violence, rage, horror, personal inspiration, savagery, war, myth, epical stuff, the slaughter, the deep spiritual horror.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T05:43:54-07:00","id":1134809,"title":"","content":"Its pure addiction and love on the first sight.<br /> No other game managed to keep me and my party for so long time and so deep inside its world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-28-2017, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T21:41:39-07:00","id":1135347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1134719#post1134719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I love the spiritual nature of the Garou. As a person, I love being in nature, and seeing the beauty of the Earth. Having a setting where the Earth is literally alive, and your purpose is to protect that speaks to me. The fact that it's also mixed with a horror setting, which happens to be my favorite genre just doubles up on two things that I've always appreciated.<br /> <br /> I also feel like Werewolf allows for a large variety of subject matter for storylines. You can have internal or external Sept politics. You can have the body horror/slash em up style of gameplay. You can have characters caught between their dual natures of having once been human (If you're a Homid born) and you're new life as a monster, dealing with the Rage burning inside of you. You can have adventures into the Near Realms or Deep Umbra that can hit on nearly any topic you want. And while other game settings can have these types of stories as well, I feel like the game gives you near endless possibilities while keeping a unique theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. The environmentalism angle really did speak to me back in the day (and still does), it was partly what steered me to the direction my college studies went and the other parts were very fascinating too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T04:55:00-07:00","id":1135392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta#post1133131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm actually DON'T like Garou. On the hater level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why you actually don't like Garou ? They are awesome !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-30-2017, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T01:12:35-07:00","id":1135697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135392#post1135392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why you actually don't like Garou ? They are awesome !</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Their hypocrisy (the world become such shitty place cuz of them mostly)<br /> 2) Bigotry and racism (toward many Fera, many other supers - esp vampires)<br /> 3) They like to act as they are big shit, but they have no actual crossover wins? On the high level they seem to be weak.<br /> 4) Their constant whining is just annoying.<br /> after all, for me they are really like those school nerds who one day came to school with guns.<br /> I will be glad to see them like this cuz this how they deserved feel themselves: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rc2OvrpzjvM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rc2OvrpzjvM</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T03:45:18-07:00","id":1135724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135697#post1135697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Their hypocrisy (the world become such shitty place cuz of them mostly)<br /> 2) Bigotry and racism (toward many Fera, many other supers - esp vampires)<br /> 3) They like to act as they are big shit, but they have no actual crossover wins? On the high level they seem to be weak.<br /> 4) Their constant whining is just annoying.<br /> after all, for me they are really like those school nerds who one day came to school with guns.<br /> I will be glad to see them like this cuz this how they deserved feel themselves: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rc2OvrpzjvM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rc2OvrpzjvM</a></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Not all garou are hypocrites, there are many among them, including our player characters and many signature characters, who are actually models of of honesty, for the good or for the worse, yes there is still hypocrisy inside the garou society related to the devastating mistakes they have done to the past and still do but there is also great valor, heroism and sacrifice, something that is vastly missing from all other splats. Afterall all WoD games have hipocrisy inside them.<br /> <br /> And no, the world did not become bad only because of the garou, if the weaver did not make the wyrm mad, the werewoles would not have been created by Gaia and their Rage would not have been tainted by the corrupting wyrm. In the WoD the major reaponsibility for a bad world falls to mankind, humans are to blame for all that is bad, the impergium may be the reason, but the last hit has been delivered by mankind who only made a step further to make the world even worse. The proof is the modern day life that enslaved mankind into prisons if glass and metal poluting the very world they live in. You know, only the garou care for the future of the natural world, and from the other splats only very few who still can't do the difference. Even the other fera are incapable to protect the earth from the danger of msnkind, at least werewolves try.<br /> <br /> 2)Yes werewolves are full of bigotry and racism, but their enemies are full of bigotry and racism against them too. And the other fera were ill-mannered towards the Garou even before the war of Rage. This is the nature of nature and this is the nature of nature's shapeshifting children, your blood my life, your devastation my presevation, its only natural that kind of manner to extend to in their society and their religion. A religion that proves true though, look what humans do to the world, look what the children of the wyrm do to mother earth, so yes Garou have a plenty of reasons to be violent both righteous and wicked ones. <br /> <br /> Vampires? But vampires are the personification of racism, ''humanity is inferior'' I hear it in every game I have ever played, not to mention the various supplements. <br /> Garou have every righteous reason to be hateful against vampires, they spread disease and put family in danger, not to mention that their very presence is blasphemy. The werewooves only want to return the walking corpses to the earth they belong, its simple logic not racism.<br /> <br /> 3)Come on lets don't be hypocrites, everyone would like to act big if he/she was actually big, muscular and fluffy. Appart from that I don't really remember any splat to ever have a clean victory over another splat. And for good reason, after all each game is its own game and it would have been really bad to be depicted as inferior towards another game. So yes garou are presented as having no crossover victories, but no other species do so as well.<br /> <br /> From my experience with all wod games I can say with the hand in my heart that Garou on high level can fight against anything of higher level, its just that high level garou fight completely differently than low level ones and with more sophisticated methods and adapt completely differently to the various challenges. I had some extremely awesome experiences against demons, mages mathusela vamps and various other higher level entities, (our Rank3 ragabash killed a nictuku with one arrow shot).<br /> <br /> 4)What do you mean about constant whinning ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T05:22:07-07:00","id":1135738,"title":"","content":"1) They lost and lost and lost grounds. Imperium made people against nature, War of Rage eliminate a lot potential allies. Even now they continue to fight each other and to be complete dicks.The protection of Earth was their duty and they failed. Hence, the modern world is completely their fault.<br /> 2) F*ck humans they ARE inferior. Mages, fairies and others don't hate vampires that much. Only Garou do. And they don't even try to make difference. That's wrong.<br /> And vampires don't care about werewolves till they try to fight them without any reason.<br /> 3) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yes Garou are presented as having no crossover victories, but no other species do so as well </div> </div> </div> Techs and katayans killed freaking Ravana.<br /> 4) &quot;Oh-h, that's so bad&quot; &quot;Oh-h no one like us&quot; Yep, and you deserve this.i want.<br /> that's why I like to see them as broken and destroyed as Rambo on the vid. They should suffer. Till any piece of hope and happiness will be destroyed in them. That's what I want.<br /> UPD: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> its just that high level garou fight completely differently than low level ones and with more sophisticated methods and adapt completely differently to the various challenges. </div> </div> </div> Other supers - like vampire Elders and old mages, fairies - has enough raw power usually. Also, Garou can't be immortal or at least long-living - that's sucks, cuz any other splat can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 08-31-2017, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T11:29:04-07:00","id":1135852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135738#post1135738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) They lost and lost and lost grounds. Imperium made people against nature, War of Rage eliminate a lot potential allies. Even now they continue to fight each other and to be complete dicks.The protection of Earth was their duty and they failed. Hence, the modern world is completely their fault.<br /> 2) F*ck humans they ARE inferior. Mages, fairies and others don't hate vampires that much. Only Garou do. And they don't even try to make difference. That's wrong.<br /> And vampires don't care about werewolves till they try to fight them without any reason.<br /> 3) Techs and katayans killed freaking Ravana.<br /> 4) &quot;Oh-h, that's so bad&quot; &quot;Oh-h no one like us&quot; Yep, and you deserve this.i want.<br /> that's why I like to see them as broken and destroyed as Rambo on the vid. They should suffer. Till any piece of hope and happiness will be destroyed in them. That's what I want.<br /> UPD: Other supers - like vampire Elders and old mages, fairies - has enough raw power usually. Also, Garou can't be immortal or at least long-living - that's sucks, cuz any other splat can.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1)Yes garou made grave mistakes and they lost ground because of the failings of the past, and here we have a wonderfully brilliand twist, the generation of the apocalypse! A whole modern time generation of garou who want to right the wrongs of their ancestors, they may be too late or they may be indeed the heroes who will make the difference, And this element is WONDERFUL to run in a campaign. Also they are the only ones who actively do something to protect the earth, and by something I mean risking limb and life.<br /> Vampires: earth ? what earth ? you mean earth meld ? no? pff don't bother<br /> Mages: what the earth is alive ? wuaaaauuu illuminatiooon, zeeennnn, oooommmmm<br /> Fera: the earth is dying? to the %&amp;*!@ wiith you, may the wyrm take you too<br /> Changelings: the earth is dying ? AAAAA THE EARTH IS DYIIIIING, there will be no more dreaming <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ''whimp whimp''<br /> <br /> You see maybe in older times the garou were seemed to be idiotic, but in the modern world its exactly the opposite, can't say the same for the other splats though. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The modern world is completely their fault? Now thats an exaggeration, greater responsibility falls to the kindred who corrupted mankind from within through their various political schemings over so many millenia. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> 2) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">F*ck humans they ARE inferior</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>, thats racist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Garou have every reason to hate vampires, man even I as human would hate a walking corpse that wants to drink my blood, burn the forest of my village because his elder wants to expand his domain or even trying to turn me in a walking corpse that drinks blood and put in danger all those who are close to me because of my unholy hunger. Not to mention again that vampires spread diseases, enter wyrm ridden frenzies of blood lust, spread wyrm taint that attracts other wyrm thing etc etc. Immagine now the righteous hate of a Rage fuelled beast for the undead. Its the kindred who should already start to make the difference, if they were not do wyrmie thing Garou would automatically leave them alone.<br /> <br /> 3)Oh man you say it on your own <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Techs <b>AND</b> kathayans, its not a single splat thing and it was not a victory, more like the remaining survivors of a nuclear holocaust.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> 4)Come onnnn, you exaggerate, there is no whinning in the Garou only bad grudge. Afterall its the fera's fault that can't see in what times they live in, and idiotic enough not to come in terms with their wolf cousins, only after they lost their caerns to the wyrm they came crawling to the garou pleading for acceptance and the garou did offer hospitality and aid.<br /> <br /> 5) Other supers may have raw power but garou have ways to take that power away from them. And garou can become immortal, its just that when they do so they stop being garou and become something else, from mythical godlike beings to spirits and incarna like entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-31-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T12:14:51-07:00","id":1135864,"title":"","content":"1) Pff. And why they couldn't be someone who didn't make this amount if mess&gt; Still hope that may be 5th ed retcon some of their fails...<br /> 2)as well as their hate to vampires. We as players know that at least Camarilia bloodsakers in-mass are mostly normal guys, and all this connection to Wyrm is just shit from old 1st ed days.<br /> 3) OK who Garou killed with help of fairies? <br /> 4) So, Fera should be nice to those who slayed almost all their kind? F*ck this. Really, the World with such protectors dosn't deserve to exist. It's better to be kings in hell<br /> 5) So, Garou are officially inferior race thins other splats can be more powerfull.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And garou can become immortal, its just that when they do so they stop being garou and become something else, from mythical godlike beings to spirits and incarna like entities. </div> </div> </div>What do you mean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T13:41:20-07:00","id":1135912,"title":"","content":"1) I am not sure if they will change the history, the only thing so far is the mood, when will you rage and that the apocalypse will be something that will be real or false depending on the story teller or something like that.<br /> <br /> 2)No, camarilla are not normal guys, they pretend they are, they are still rutheless monsters that cling to humanity only in order not to lose themselves entirely to the beast, even toreador who are admirers of humanity time and again don't actually love it. Imagine the worse of the camarilla how worse they can be. They are just not sabbat nuttshellheads.<br /> The garou don't usually smell wyrm on vampires physically, usually, They mostly smell it with the sense wyrm gift which automatically makes them target because vampires do spread corruption. Unfortunately for vampires the wyrm touches anything in the matterial world that represents its presence or its nature, the same happens with werewolves that eat people or enter the thrall of the wyrm.<br /> It doesn't really have to do with the edition of the game, its just how the wyrm enters in your very being.<br /> <br /> 3)The fomorian king Balor. You know, Balor's gaze. Along with his fomorian army.<br /> You know Balor was a giant, if not titan, of unimaginable power.<br /> <br /> 4)No, the fera shouldn't be nice to those who slayed almost all their kind, but they should also be open-minded to what really is happening around them.<br /> <br /> 5)What do you mean by inferior? I don't think the other splats are more powerfull, they are just seem to look like that but they aren't really as powerful as they claim to be.<br /> High arete mages can still burn themselves up with their own spells and vampire elders can still be killed by human ninjas, what do you mean by ''more powerful'' ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do you mean </div> </div> </div>That garou can become immortal, its rare but it has happened, like when they get transformed to other kind of creatures through legendary gifts, ot they turn litteraly immortal by residing for long time in the umbra and turn to spirits, or by ascendig by Gaia (or the Wyrm) to incarna like beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-31-2017, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:12:26-07:00","id":1135922,"title":"","content":"1) I agree with you but I still hope.<br /> 2) Again, I still hope they will changed it. Sense Wyrm does not shows mages and fairies, you know? Let's no put this shit to vamps. We live in freackin PC-era.<br /> 3) Proof? Seriously know, I never heard about this.<br /> 4) After what this motherf*ckers did? I think for average Fera, garou should suffer than crawl - for long time. For all the shit Garou did to them and to the whole world.<br /> 5) When they fight against same-level creature from other splut they do not need to use tactics that much. No, I like and respect tacticians, but if you need it more than you enemies - you are weak and inferior creature.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:28:11-07:00","id":1135928,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta#post1133131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are such topics in Exalted section, so I want to start this one. I'm actually DON'T like Garou. On the hater level. But... I would like to ead about why people can root to them.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">This is a complicated question because what are you asking? why do we like the Garou or WtA: the game? </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Because thats two different answers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif, serif, EmojiFont\">Why i like WtA? Because is the best game about hubris from OPP/WW. Unlike other OPP games about hubris the important thing to remember about privilege/hubris is that you dont need cosmic power to drive the point home, you just need contrast and said contrast is inescapable and subtle in their relationship with their kinfolk and the effect Garou society have on the garou themselves that puts them in a position of privilege and power with little accountability. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif, serif, EmojiFont\">Obviously thats no the themes the authors went for it but something i have learned is that the authors intend on OPP games is to be ignored because people do come with better ones. The technocracy as an example, in their their falling in drive the point they wanted to make home made mage a better games by accident more than by design.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">So on WtA, what i like is on one part the contrast that shines through of a society of barbarians in modern times. The game has a timeless theme of &quot;Good intention dont make you a good guy&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> The fact that the Garou nation while having a objectively good goal (saving the world) is so flaw, to me, is part of the meat of the game. You (the player) are part of the Garou nation and have to work alongside it. There is decent people in it but also plenty (like a whole tribe name the fianna) of either useless assholes and the crux of the argument is how much you gonna compromise to achieve your goal.<br /> <br /> You can always take the moral high ground and draw your line on the sand and say &quot;no, screw you guys&quot; but that doesnt help anyone on the long term really. You become a foot note on the Garou nation history and said Garou nation continues to be as shitty as it is.<br /> <br /> I have a post that i explain my appeal of WtA the game in a very inspired frenzy of words but paraphrasing<br /> <br /> &quot;That for me is the horror of werewolf the decision you make and how seductive the garou society is for a garou. &quot;Be a good crusader, kill the wyrm and anything standing in your way and you will get honor, power and be a hero and be right....just dont think too much. Live fast and die young in the name of our war without changing a damn thing of this vicious circle and then an eternity in valhalla awaits you&quot; thats the speech of the garou nation at large. And the horror comes on how many garou buy it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135724#post1135724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)Yes werewolves are full of bigotry and racism, but their enemies are full of bigotry and racism against them too. And the other fera were ill-mannered towards the Garou even before the war of Rage. This is the nature of nature and this is the nature of nature's shapeshifting children, your blood my life, your devastation my presevation, its only natural that kind of manner to extend to in their society and their religion. A religion that proves true though, look what humans do to the world, look what the children of the wyrm do to mother earth, so yes Garou have a plenty of reasons to be violent both righteous and wicked ones.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Wow.....thats.....just wow..... Well this is an example of the Garou indoctrination. Where ill-manners justifies extinction war......wow. No, just no. Garou arent right nor justified by any definition of the word even the setting both acknowledges that and even by the standard of their religion they were out of place on the war of Rage. By the standard of their religion Gaia is all knowing and all wise, yet the garou decided they knew better than her when she appointed them for a specific role and they took all the roles as defenders of Gaia from the other fera. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Also, crossover aside funnily enough thats not true. The enemies of the Garou, the Black Spiral Dancers, are way more tolerant and accepting than the Garou themselves. They will take anyone who would walk the spiral and they will kill and possibly skull fuck (maybe not in that order) anyone even themselves. So in a twisted way they are equal opportunist skull-fuckers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135697#post1135697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) They like to act as they are big shit, but they have no actual crossover wins? On the high level they seem to be weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Cannon crossovers are bullshit from the get got anyway. Any metaplot involving crossover is mostly decided by what splat is more popular (or the need of the metaplot) than by any degree of common sense. You got things like Blood Treachery which made 0 sense in so many ways but was decided because vampires were more popular than mages. If your measure of how good a game is by how it matches in canon crossover that's your prerogative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135852#post1135852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see maybe in older times the garou were seemed to be idiotic, but in the modern world its exactly the opposite, can't say the same for the other splats though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Garou as whole both ancient and modern are still idiotic because they are a product of their society. A society that glorifies sacrifice in battle and shuns other option with dealing with problems, a dogmatic society that chew young garou and makes them not question the glorified past. A society that gives garou an easy out because in the end they are scare of living, its drills into their heads that war is all they are in for and thus most young garou are scare of having to live and probe that they arent as good as their society makes them to be. So it makes songs about dying in glorious battle and Garou die content they die with honor and shove the problems that plague them are for the next ones to deal with.<br /> <br /> The struggle of the Garou is whats good about them. Is living in this society that tempts you so much with glory, purpose and privilege as long as you dont question it but at the same times fails in making things better. Is trying to improve the Garou nation one small battle at the time while compromising yourself just a little more. Make the hard choices just so things are a little easier for the next generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-31-2017, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:37:13-07:00","id":1135933,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135864#post1135864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2)as well as their hate to vampires. We as players know that at least Camarilia bloodsakers in-mass are mostly normal guys, and all this connection to Wyrm is just shit from old 1st ed days.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135912#post1135912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2)No, camarilla are not normal guys, they pretend they are, they are still rutheless monsters that cling to humanity only in order not to lose themselves entirely to the beast, even toreador who are admirers of humanity time and again don't actually love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. 100% agreed that the Cam is not just a bunch of &quot;mostly normal guys&quot;. That statement isn't remotely true. You can't list has-to-eat-people as just some sort of alternative-diet. It's a fact of Vampire existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135912#post1135912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The garou don't usually smell wyrm on vampires physically, usually, They mostly smell it with the sense wyrm gift which automatically makes them target because vampires do spread corruption. Unfortunately for vampires the wyrm touches anything in the matterial world that represents its presence or its nature, the same happens with werewolves that eat people or enter the thrall of the wyrm.<br /> It doesn't really have to do with the edition of the game, its just how the wyrm enters in your very being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting, Garou <u>never</u> physically smell Wyrm-taint on people. Wyrm-taint isn't a physical thing. And it makes complete sense why Vampires should smell of the Wyrm within the Werewolf cosmology. Even Vampires admit/think they're cursed. They have the Beast riding them, driving them to commit inhumane acts of violence and degradation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135864#post1135864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) So, Fera should be nice to those who slayed almost all their kind? F*ck this. Really, the World with such protectors dosn't deserve to exist. It's better to be kings in hell</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in fairness, that slaying took place in prehistory (mostly). And issues have popped up in more recent history, but generally at least a couple of hundred years ago. At some point, yea the Fera and the Garou should realize the world is at stake and work together. Harboring grudges at the cost of the literal world is pretty dumb (from both sides).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135922#post1135922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2) Again, I still hope they will changed it. Sense Wyrm does not shows mages and fairies, you know? Let's no put this shit to vamps. We live in freackin PC-era.<br /> 3) Proof? Seriously know, I never heard about this.<br /> 4) After what this motherf*ckers did? I think for average Fera, garou should suffer than crawl - for long time. For all the shit Garou did to them and to the whole world.<br /> 5) When they fight against same-level creature from other splut they do not need to use tactics that much. No, I like and respect tacticians, but if you need it more than you enemies - you are weak and inferior creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>2) Sense Wyrm has nothing to do with a &quot;PC-era&quot;. It senses soul corruption. Mages in general don't suffer from it. Nephandi do. Some Changelings even do, but in general they don't because they shouldn't in-Setting. I'm not sure why the idea of Wyrm-taint bothers you so much.<br /> 3) Balor was part of Changeling/Fianna backstory stuff.<br /> 4) And that's the sort of thought process that leads to the WoD being in the state it's in.<br /> 5) This is just silly. Being a pack creature does not make an individual &quot;inferior&quot;. What does that even mean? WoD doesn't have &quot;levels&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-01-2017, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:41:32-07:00","id":1135935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The struggle of the Garou is whats good about them. Is living in this society that tempts you so much with glory, purpose and privilege as long as you dont question it but at the same times fails in making things better. Is trying to improve the Garou nation one small battle at the time while compromising yourself just a little more. Make the hard choices just so things are a little easier for the next generation. </div> </div> </div> Yep. That's why I so like to see Garou when they suffer like Rambo from st Blood. Broken, despaired, who thought they tried their best but who got in fact only pain and and suffers. Cuz what they deserve.<br /> Seriously, something on this level of despair (look at the girl's eyes)<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hV4z64tfhU8\" data-code=\"hV4z64tfhU8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/hV4z64tfhU8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 08-31-2017, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:11:20-07:00","id":1135953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135935#post1135935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yep. That's why I so like to see Garou when they suffer like Rambo from st Blood. Broken, despaired, who thought they tried their best but who got in fact only pain and and suffers. Cuz what they deserve.<br /> Seriously, something on this level of despair (look at the girl's eyes)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooookaay *slightly steps away* i think we have a miss-understanding here. My point was that the meat of the game doesnt come from battle or even physical violence (or even the threat of death) but from the struggle of working with people you find morally objectionable in the hopes of changing things. It doesnt come from one big battle against the wyrm (which i would argue is not even that important) but from the small victories. The small changes that may build up to large changes in the Nation.<br /> <br /> Is not about terror, or being broken or even despair but about seeing the Wheel the garou have trapped themselves into and decide whether to join them or try to change the wheel. Is about risking doing things that may risk branding you a coward, a society of warriors, not only to your contemporaries but your future generations.<br /> <br /> Because even if you &quot;First blood-them like Rambo from st Blood. Broken, despaired, who thought they tried their best but who got in fact only pain and and suffers. Cuz what they deserve.&quot; Thats what the Garou are conditioned to think is a good dead. Dying in battle is a warriors death, even resisting torture is doing their duty and thats a good way to go for them.<br /> <br /> The average Garou would die and said to himself &quot;well at least i honored my ancestor&quot; and be content without ever thinking that there might have been a better way.<br /> <br /> As a side note, you seem to have a fixation or at least a axe to grind with the Garou being tortured. So why make a thread about why people like the Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-31-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:41:13-07:00","id":1135971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135953#post1135953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooookaay *slightly steps away* i think we have a miss-understanding here.<br /> The average Garou would die and said to himself &amp;quot;well at least i honored my ancestor&amp;quot; and be content without ever thinking that there might have been a better way. <br /> <br /> As a side note, you seem to have a fixation or at least a axe to grind with the Garou being tortured. So why make a thread about why people like the Garou? </div> </div> </div> </div>In turn my point is also not _only_ about tortures (at least not about physical ones). It's also about shame depression, despair and mental suffering. When you think you tried you best and you really did - but no.For all your work people will spit in your face. All your sacrificesupport were for nothing. You have no one and nothing. It'seems about something deeply destructive. If I can be poetic a bit - sone thing what will burn your soul out of you and slowly broke. Physical pain is a good thing for it bUT is not the main part. <br /> That'said what I wish for Garou. <br /> As for why I started this thread - cuz I used to like WtA when I just found out about Word. Then they dissapointed me very hard. And I really can't see how people can like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T16:23:03-07:00","id":1135990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135971#post1135971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I really can't see how people can like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked why people like it.<br /> <br /> People give you reasons(LOTS of them).<br /> <br /> You still fail to understand.<br /> <br /> End the thread? <br /> <br /> Because now I'm not exactly sure what you're trying to accomplish here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T19:48:16-07:00","id":1136058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135697#post1135697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Their hypocrisy (the world become such shitty place cuz of them mostly)</div> </div> </div> </div>A common failing of large-scale societies. Just consider how much more hypocritical humanity is when it gets a good deal and rests on it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Bigotry and racism (toward many Fera, many other supers - esp vampires) </div> </div> </div>Not getting along with the Fera is a deep flaw that the game presents as in need of reconciling if anything is actually going to get done. However, one should note that killing vampires isn't bigotry - it's pest control.<br /> <br /> And even vampires would probably agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) They like to act as they are big shit, but they have no actual crossover wins? On the high level they seem to be weak. </div> </div> </div>The shaky and cracktastic nature of crossovers having been discussed already, one should note that they have taken care of problems of their own. The Storm Eater of the Old West and Seventh Generation cult, for example. Also, on a day to day basis, I don't think that vampires or mages would fair too well against fomori, gorgons, or drones in the numbers that the world seems to throw the way of the werewolves. Hell, Mage even dummies down normal spirit attack damage from aggravated to lethal in its core, explicitly citing that the Werewolf approach is too dangerous for mages to deal with on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T01:10:36-07:00","id":1136112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135697#post1135697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Their hypocrisy (the world become such shitty place cuz of them mostly)<br /> 2) Bigotry and racism (toward many Fera, many other supers - esp vampires)<br /> 3) They like to act as they are big shit, but they have no actual crossover wins? On the high level they seem to be weak.<br /> 4) Their constant whining is just annoying.<br /> after all, for me they are really like those school nerds who one day came to school with guns.<br /> I will be glad to see them like this cuz this how they deserved feel themselves: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rc2OvrpzjvM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rc2OvrpzjvM</a><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it only make it cooler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T03:00:05-07:00","id":1136124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1135990#post1135990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asked why people like it.<br /> <br /> People give you reasons(LOTS of them).<br /> <br /> You still fail to understand.<br /> <br /> End the thread? <br /> <br /> Because now I'm not exactly sure what you're trying to accomplish here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I answered LokiRaven question.<br /> I get the reasons, i just still can't get how them overcome all the flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T03:29:05-07:00","id":1136129,"title":"","content":"Anyway for me the main issue is that Garou was presented as the good guys. AFAIK there was even commercial for environmental protection organisations in WtA books of first edition. Really? These assholes are poster-boys? Who made a FEW genocides and completely failed their mission. They are not Heroes. That's why I'd like to them suffering.<br /> UPD: What is the biggest werewolves wins? Balor and 7th Generation Cult. What else? I mean canonical wins, without which Apocalypses could start early?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-01-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T04:37:55-07:00","id":1136138,"title":"","content":"Storm Eater, Kupala, THE EATER OF SOULS ''Dood that's even better than killing an antediluvean''. Probably Set. And many many other wonderful enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T04:58:04-07:00","id":1136142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kupala </div> </div> </div> Tzimizy saved him (I like this guys))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:25:08-07:00","id":1136157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136142#post1136142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tzimizy saved him (I like this guys))</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially, hi<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">s ritual never finished-succeeded-whatever.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 09-01-2017, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:06:28-07:00","id":1136171,"title":"","content":"Look...<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4950\" data-vbnamecard=\"4950\">Lashet</a>. No one is going to convince you to like the Garou. I personally don't care if you do. I doubt any others really do. But it seems an odd place to come (the Werewolf forums) to gripe about them and go on and on about how you want them to suffer (which is a bit creepy).<br /> <br /> In Setting they are the heroes, even if they're tragic ones. The failings of the past only feed into what the stakes of the Apocalypse are. They've had more than a few major setbacks. But trying to write off or outright ignoring they're victories (which <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a> listed some) seems intellectually dishonest. *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:37:37-07:00","id":1136186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But trying to write off or outright ignoring they're victories (which <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a> listed some) seems intellectually dishonest. </div> </div> </div> I ignored only Kupala since it's hardly epic win. I would be glad to know anything also.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Setting they are the heroes, even if they're tragic ones. </div> </div> </div> Only from their POV. I we look at WoD as at setting, there is another (lot of them). + just common sense (after all this fails...)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The failings of the past only feed into what the stakes of the Apocalypse are. </div> </div> </div> And it's all their fault. Don't blame humankind. Humans acted just like humans. Garou could not wait anything else from humanity (esp after Imperium). Garou should consider this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> how you want them to suffer (which is a bit creepy). </div> </div> </div>As for me, they deserved it more than any other splat. For all mess their people did. Make them like Jayne Pool after &quot;honeymoon&quot; (this! i won't disturb you with this comparisons anymore - seems I found a god example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-01-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:38:40-07:00","id":1136187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136138#post1136138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storm Eater, Kupala, THE EATER OF SOULS ''Dood that's even better than killing an antediluvean''. Probably Set. And many many other wonderful enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talons of the Wyrm and Zmei, too. Generally, though, this is meant to be something that player characters do, so the spotlight isn't very hogged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-01-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T07:48:04-07:00","id":1136189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136186#post1136186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I ignored only Kupala since it's hardly epic win. I would be glad to know anything also.<br /> Only from their POV. I we look at WoD as at setting, there is another (lot of them). + just common sense (after all this fails...)</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mage only makes sense for Mage. You can be a hero in Werewolf, if you make the effort to do it. In Vampire, you're still stuck being a net negative no matter what you do, because it's entirely constructed around giving up and just riding things out for as long as you can. This is Vampire's thing, and it's welcome to it, but other games have other priorities and setups. If you don't like them, do what I do and quietly write them out of your games, homebrew material that you produce, whatever. When it comes to aggressive visitors coming by to lob a hot mess of hate, though, I'm rather tired of having to re-enact my earliest days on the WW forums, and I don't think I'm alone in this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's all their fault. Don't blame humankind. Humans acted just like humans. Garou could not wait anything else from humanity (esp after Imperium). Garou should consider this. </div> </div> </div>The Impergium was thousands of years ago. You can't keep riding that shit as an excuse on either front.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for me, they deserved it more than any other splat. For all mess their people did. </div> </div> </div>More than Vampires and Mages? You do realize that each game presents the characters as being in a society that has fucked up, right? Garou are even more down on themselves for it, but vampires just shrug and stop caring if they even ever cared to begin with, and mages are likely to see things they did that were horrible as necessary or even positive. Even the fae that the changelings venerate as their ancestors fucked up terribly, given the recent Dark Ages WoD offering from not too long ago, slinging around weaponized sources of Banality against each other until it came back to bite them in the ass so hard they had to either hide in human reincarnation processes or flee the world for Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T08:12:48-07:00","id":1136197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136187#post1136187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Talons of the Wyrm and Zmei, too. Generally, though, this is meant to be something that player characters do, so the spotlight isn't very hogged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but there is one case that a signature character single handendly deals with one of the talons,<br /> I am looking at you Evan Heals the Past <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the zmei, GLORY TO THE TVARIVICH !!! ummm sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 09-01-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T08:16:50-07:00","id":1136199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Impergium </div> </div> </div> Even without Impergium. humans acted as usually, when destroyed environment. That's is just human nature, and Garou needed to think about it. (besides, environmental issues seems to be overused and boring plotline today... but that's just IMHO)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than Vampires and Mages? </div> </div> </div> They neither heroes nor pretend to be. Yep, they are egoists and assholes, but it's not that bad. When they want to attack someone, that cuz some practical goals.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mages are likely to see things they did that were horrible </div> </div> </div> Like what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:55:32-07:00","id":1136225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136199#post1136199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even without Impergium. humans acted as usually, when destroyed environment. That's is just human nature, and Garou needed to think about it. (besides, environmental issues seems to be overused and boring plotline today... but that's just IMHO)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that true, WtA fails to address environmental issues in a good way however i argue that is not important. Environmentalism is just a narrative tool of a &quot;objectively good goal&quot; that the game needs to Juxtapose with the actions of the garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136199#post1136199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They neither heroes nor pretend to be. Yep, they are egoists and assholes, but it's not that bad. When they want to attack someone, that cuz some practical goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know the Traditions are painted as heroes, dont you? The justify their actions as for the &quot;greater good&quot; same with the technocracy. Even the camarilla paint itself as a holding the line from the chaos that is the sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:11:19-07:00","id":1136229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136225#post1136225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes that true, WtA fails to address environmental issues in a good way however i argue that is not important. Environmentalism is just a narrative tool of a &quot;objectively good goal&quot; that the game needs to Juxtapose with the actions of the garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... wow.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You do know the Traditions are painted as heroes, dont you? The justify their actions as for the &quot;greater good&quot; same with the technocracy. Even the camarilla paint itself as a holding the line from the chaos that is the sabbat.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> Are them? Camarilia is more like lesser evil. Mages more like researchers and explorers. Anyway, they don't beat themselves in chests about 'how heroic and good and tragic we are'.<br /> Btw, at least Technocracy really did and do something useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-01-2017, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:21:17-07:00","id":1136237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136229#post1136229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, they don't beat themselves in chests about 'how heroic and good and tragic&quot; we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do. The whole ascension war is full of both side thinking they are doing the heroic and good thing for the reality. Up until revised when it didnt matter anymore the Ascension war was something that defined mage society.<br /> <br /> But you seem confused or at least undecided on what you are talking about. Are you talking about IC or OOC when you said how the garou &quot;beat themselves in chests about 'how heroic and good and tragic they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> Simply put, is your issue that the game itself, as fiction, paints the Garou as objectively good or that the garou (as character in a world) paint themselves as good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-01-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:48:15-07:00","id":1136254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136237#post1136237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, is your issue that the game itself, as fiction, paints the Garou as objectively good or that the garou (as character in a world) paint themselves as good?</div> </div> </div> </div> Both + the fact that vampire-fans and haters single-handly put me down about Garou and I could not objectively answer them anything, cuz they were right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T11:47:30-07:00","id":1136292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136254#post1136254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Both + the fact that vampire-fans and haters single-handly put me down about Garou and I could not objectively answer them anything, cuz they were right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay i cant help you with the fact that vampire fan and haters of the game soured you to WtA. Honestly, if your opinion is so easily sway then thats a thing that you (with or without proffesional help) need to handle if you feel thats a problem in a better place than a forum.<br /> <br /> Now on IC. IC Garou are no different from the other 2 main splats. They all sell themselves as the good guys and for their society to function that label needs to remain there. Is no different than the camarilla/sabbat saying they are better option than the other or the traditions and technocracy`s ascension war in which each side is the &quot;good one&quot; in their point of view.<br /> <br /> OOC however the game says this &quot;Garou are the heroes of the story but they arent exactly morally good&quot; the game, likely by accident, makes the point that just because one is &quot;fighting the good fight&quot; that doesnt mean one is justified in their actions. Even if the garou pc is good he still have to work alongside people with dubious morality/detrimental to their cause and learn to work alongside those characters.<br /> <br /> I like to compare WtA as the walking dead. The meaty enemy of the nation isnt the wyrm just like the interesting enemy on the show/comic isnt the zombies itself but the other survivors who all have a good motivation (survive) but their dubious method bring the protagonist in conflict with them but at the same time the zombies forces them to cooperate for their survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-01-2017, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T12:09:55-07:00","id":1136298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay i cant help you with the fact that vampire fan and haters of the game soured you to WtA. Honestly, if your opinion is so easily sway then that a thing that you (with or without proffesional help) need to handle or not in a better place than a forum </div> </div> </div> &quot;They are fanatics who killed vampires even on 6th Humanity while do the same thing&quot; - so what can I answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T12:22:16-07:00","id":1136303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136298#post1136298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;They are fanatics who killed vampires even on 6th Humanity while do the same thing&quot; - so what can I answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;While do the same thing&quot;? Can you edit that for clarity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-01-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T12:28:02-07:00","id":1136307,"title":"","content":"Here's a question, -why- is enviromentalism a bad thing to focus on? Even if it seems trite, it doesn't mean it is not a huge issue even in our world. Species die, or resources are wasted on species that could not adapt. Nature can adapt, sure, but that doesn't mean worry over it and helping is not important.<br /> <br /> Captain Planet stuff or not, I like that WtA goes out and says that we should be responsible and care about things. Not just the enviroment, but those hurt by corruption is social services, the police, the corporations and so on. After all, huge part of the fight against Wyrm is also -preventing- taint from seeping too deep and that means helping those in need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T12:44:03-07:00","id":1136320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136303#post1136303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;While do the same thing&quot;? Can you edit that for clarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>They kill people and sometimes eat them. Like.. you know vampires did. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">After all, huge part of the fight against Wyrm is also -preventing- taint from seeping too deep and that means helping those in need.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>in their actions.And it's hard to fight any normal strategy about their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T12:46:37-07:00","id":1136321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136199#post1136199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even without Impergium. humans acted as usually, when destroyed environment. That's is just human nature, and Garou needed to think about it. (besides, environmental issues seems to be overused and boring plotline today... but that's just IMHO)</div> </div> </div> </div>So... are you agreeing with me, then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They neither heroes nor pretend to be. Yep, they are egoists and assholes, but it's not that bad. When they want to attack someone, that cuz some practical goals. </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't even make an attempt and see nothing wrong with making the world shittier for their own benefit; you can at least appeal to some ideals that Garou would have to do something about a problem and hope for an outcome. I'd rather have an afflicted party member in the Darkest Dungeon than one that flat out goes to the other side before the Siren even sings.<br /> <br /> As for Mages, they do claim to be heroes, as noted above. Mage leans rather heavily on that notion, in fact. However, as you noted in identifying mages as explorers...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like what? </div> </div> </div>Explorers are fairly well-known for having committed horrible atrocities on indigenous people that they &quot;discovered&quot;, plundering wealth and important cultural artifacts, and marking land for &quot;development&quot;. Christopher Columbus, for example, went around torturing, killing, and raping Arawak before turning his gaze to Africa for slave labor. This is the sort of low road you find in Mage. You'll reach a juncture where a mage has to decide whether or not they'll break a few eggs to further their goals. Frequently, they will break even more than they need to just to make sure; the Technocracy is infamous for this, particularly since they were backing a lot of historical explorers, but the Traditions aren't exactly averse to trying to absorb other groups of people and use them as political pawns to strengthen their particular Tradition. As far as allies go, the Traditions are not particularly nice ones, but they talk a big game about fighting against the Technocracy, whatever it might take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T12:51:16-07:00","id":1136326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136320#post1136320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They kill people and sometimes eat them. Like.. you know vampires did.<br /> in their actions.And it's hard to fight any normal strategy about their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cannibalism is a no-no. Anyone who makes a habit of it rather than making every earnest effort not to violate the tenet of the litany gets killed or kicked out as Ronin. Major factions that are based around it - the Maneater Bone Gnawers, Eaters of the Dead from the Silent Striders, and, of course, the fallen tribe - are also presented as antagonists. Garou also have unseen help in policing themselves in this regard, as anthropophages that do escape notice tend to get caught in the act by Corax and Nagah. The former funnel the information back to the Garou; the later make a poetic example of the careful cannibals by way of ensuring that the body is found showing evidence of having choked to death on human flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T13:05:24-07:00","id":1136338,"title":"","content":"Oh-h, after all this heroic commercials why can't Garou be like Cap America in Marvel movies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T13:15:10-07:00","id":1136342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136320#post1136320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They kill people and sometimes eat them. Like.. you know vampires did.<br /> in their actions.And it's hard to fight any normal strategy about their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted above, garou do not eat humans. It is literally against their laws to eat them, to establish how serious they are about it. Those who do are either mad, mad and seeking forbidden knowledge or whine about not being included in the discussion of laws (when they wouldn't have bothered to come to begin with). Essentially, outliers.<br /> <br /> As for their crimes, I'm getting tired of saying this but here goes; Impegrium and the War of Rage happened so long ago that the garou then -barely- resemble their modern counterparts. Modern garou have mostly owned up to these crimes and are trying their best to fix things. But still, huge part of WtA is dealing with the baggage of the past and trying to wrangle some good out of the society they have.<br /> <br /> Garou are no more evil or good than regular people, and that is a huge part of why I love the game. It actually asks you to -think- what matters and whether to just mindlessly follow the flow or actually work to make things better. Plus it brings up real issues by giving voice to those wronged without making any side purely good or evil. Werewolf is about CARING so much that it makes you angry, as the W20 kickstarter intro so well put.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T13:23:33-07:00","id":1136344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136298#post1136298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;They are fanatics who killed vampires even on 6th Humanity while do the same thing&quot; - so what can I answer?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First of all what can you answer? Do you have to answer that? What are you, Garou nation PR spoke person? I am seriously baffled that one has to &quot;defend&quot; the actions of a fictional race in RP game.<br /> <br /> But that aside humanity 6 is nothing to write home about it in term of how benign the vampire in question is and on the other hand, so what? They kill vampire regardless of their humanity (which mind you almost nobody can see) thats bad? Last time i check vampire are a parasitic race and exterminating them all is just a net win for the world. Sure there are &quot;good&quot; vampire somewhere in the world but thatsthat the same as Garou or any other splat for that matter.<br /> <br /> Hunters, in their imbued or regular variety, can also indiscriminately kill vampires. So there is little difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T17:18:48-07:00","id":1136451,"title":"","content":"Also, Garou don't typically go out of their way to kill vampires unless they have a specific reason for doing so, like having Hyperion/Katanka-Sonnak as a totem, trying to reconcile with one of the sun-aligned Fera, having an actively hostile vampire in their territory, or being a Shadow Lord or Silent Strider. Those two tribes have had it with vampires for various reasons and don't give them any quarter, though the Shadow Lords will probably try to set things up so that the vampires end up killing their own and then actively turn on each other, while the Silent Striders will go more directly Van Helsing on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T00:27:28-07:00","id":1136507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136451#post1136451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Silent Striders will go more directly Van Helsing on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But way more silently and way faster, oh and without stake guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T00:45:12-07:00","id":1136511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136451#post1136451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) having an actively hostile vampire in their territory, or being a Shadow Lord or Silent Strider. Those two tribes have had it with vampires for various reasons and don't give them any quarter, though the Shadow Lords will probably try to set things up so that the vampires end up killing their own and then actively turn on each other (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that I read somewhere, that the Shadow Lords are also likely/inclined to form understandings with the Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-02-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T02:48:53-07:00","id":1136526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136511#post1136511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that I read somewhere, that the Shadow Lords are also likely/inclined to form understandings with the Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Lords' vampire neighbours were the Tzimisce, to show where they got their view of vampires from. So they may do short time deals, but they will ALWAYS want to make sure the leech is dead in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T23:35:48-07:00","id":1136845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136344#post1136344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First of all what can you answer? Do you have to answer that? What are you, Garou nation PR spoke person? I am seriously baffled that one has to &quot;defend&quot; the actions of a fictional race in RP game.<br /> <br /> But that aside humanity 6 is nothing to write home about it in term of how benign the vampire in question is and on the other hand, so what? They kill vampire regardless of their humanity (which mind you almost nobody can see) thats bad? Last time i check vampire are a parasitic race and exterminating them all is just a net win for the world. Sure there are &quot;good&quot; vampire somewhere in the world but thatsthat the same as Garou or any other splat for that matter.<br /> <br /> Hunters, in their imbued or regular variety, can also indiscriminately kill vampires. So there is little difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were my favorite splat for that time and I couldn't sauce anything forelated their protection. And no problem, it'seems a bad thing ton kill vampire who didn't kill anyone and more moral than many humans (Humanity 6). Hunters for those guys were just a scum and fascists.<br /> Anyway, usually it'seems Garou who lose in fights with serious vampires (like Mitra).<br /> Hell the review for W20 I just read told about Garou that they are &quot;Westboro Baprist Church or SS&quot; (Idon'the know what'she worst) and it's good that there are more inteligent Feras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-03-2017, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T04:36:13-07:00","id":1136887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136845#post1136845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">didn't kill anyone and more moral than many humans (Humanity 6).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen only one player character not killing human, the only player character I ever had, and even he killed a vozjd, I didn' roll for humanity degeneration though.<br /> All other vampires I have ever seen have human fraggs, with this example I mean that a vampire who never killed humans is a rare example.<br /> Many do it and enjoy it and most do it and just don't care. Ok they don't kill babies but they don't care if they take the life of a passer by in order to gain the energy they need to hunt sabbat. The ''humanity 6'' is debatable, have you ever seen how horrible a Toreador can be with humanity 4? Camarilla Toreador I mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136845#post1136845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Anyway, usually it'seems Garou who lose in fights with serious vampires (like Mitra).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I ran a campaign related to that scenario, with Mithras buffed up. He did kill many Garou but didn't survive the fight, and I had to buff him up in order to get the scenario to the point that he did manage to kill werewolves, I used only rank one packs with rank 2 leaders and the players as full rank one pack. From the player's pack only one survived who managed to give the final blow and take Mithras's right armor gauntlet as trophy, he did lose his pack in the fight though. Howl for <b>Voice of the Fae Kin</b> ''ARRRRROOOOOOO&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T05:10:58-07:00","id":1136893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136845#post1136845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were my favorite splat for that time and I couldn't sauce anything forelated their protection. And no problem, it'seems a bad thing ton kill vampire who didn't kill anyone and more moral than many humans (Humanity 6). Hunters for those guys were just a scum and fascists.</div> </div> </div> </div>First humans dont have an humanity stat and secondly, again, how would a garou (or anyone for that matter) would know the humanity score of a vampire to know those are the rare &quot;two goody shoes&quot; vampires? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136845#post1136845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, usually it'seems Garou who lose in fights with serious vampires (like Mitra).<br /> Hell the review for W20 I just read told about Garou that they are &quot;Westboro Baprist Church or SS&quot; (Idon'the know what'she worst) and it's good that there are more inteligent Feras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we getting in yet another stupid splat dick measuring contest? Would a Garou loose against Mitras (which there is only 1 mithras in the world btw)? Depends on the build and exp of the Garou pack in question. Same as mithras could be defeated by a party of mages on arete 6+, is a very childish argument in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T05:17:16-07:00","id":1136896,"title":"","content":"THERE is a story about Mirta, but there's no story about a hogh-rank Garou who killed a lot of vampires while he was alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T05:58:36-07:00","id":1136904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136896#post1136896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THERE is a story about Mirta, but there's no story about a hogh-rank Garou who killed a lot of vampires while he was alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And your point is....?<br /> <br /> Because so far your arguments are:<br /> <br /> &quot;I dont like WtA because fan of other splats have told me they are bad&quot; which speaks more about you than WtA itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;I dont like WtA because of not many stories about them beating other splats in big battles&quot; which i already pointed out that canonical events crossover are bullshit. Also that doesnt answer the question as to why then you like Vampire when mages are clearly superior if thats what you are after.<br /> <br /> &quot;I dont like WtA because the garou nation is bad&quot; If you dont appreciate the narrative tool that the Garou nation serves then, yes you wont like WtA and nothing that we say will convince you otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-03-2017, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T08:51:13-07:00","id":1136944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136904#post1136904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And your point is....?<br /> <br /> Because so far your arguments are:<br /> <br /> &quot;I dont like WtA because fan of other splats have told me they are bad&amp;quot; which speaks more about you than WtA itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;I dont like WtA because of not many stories about them beating other splats in big battles&amp;quot; which i already pointed out that canonical events crossover are bullshit. Also that doesnt answer the question as to why then you like Vampire when mages are clearly superior if thats what you are after.<br /> <br /> &quot;I dont like WtA because the garou nation is bad&amp;quot; If you dont appreciate the narrative tool that the Garou nation serves then, yes you wont like WtA and nothing that we say will convince you otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting for agreement on all 3 points, especially the second one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4950\" data-vbnamecard=\"4950\">Lashet</a>, I'm curious why you think a pack creature should have stories of 1 on 1 victories? Also on that point, Vampires and Mages and such are not the big bads (they're really not important at all) of the Werewolf game, which is probably why Werewolf stories about them are few and far between. The closest I can think of is Baba Yaga, which the writer's introduced in Werewolf and then someone (dumbly imo) decided to kill off screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-03-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T10:31:26-07:00","id":1136959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136944#post1136944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quoting for agreement on all 3 points, especially the second one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4950\" data-vbnamecard=\"4950\">Lashet</a>, The closest I can think of is Baba Yaga</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuri the Margrave Konietzko killed a mathuselah Tzimitzki and his spawn single handendly and took his castle, before even ascending to Rank 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T12:00:11-07:00","id":1136982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136944#post1136944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious why you think a pack creature should have stories of 1 on 1 victories? Also on that point, Vampires and Mages and such are not the big bads (they're really not important at all) of the Werewolf game, which is probably why Werewolf stories about them are few and far between. The closest I can think of is Baba Yaga, which the writer's introduced in Werewolf and then someone (dumbly imo) decided to kill off screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one creature can alone <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> achive the things </span></span></span>which another must do together... yep, the first is more &quot;developed&quot;.<br /> Anyway, thanks for Konietzko! It quite helpful.<br /> OK, after all - many people like Sabbat. Ang Garou still can - and do - kill, torture and humiliate others with impunity.<br /> Kill or be killed))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-03-2017, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:31:48-07:00","id":1137131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136959#post1136959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yuri the Margrave Konietzko killed a mathuselah Tzimitzki and his spawn single handendly and took his castle, before even ascending to Rank 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I treat most of those sorts of stories the same way I treat the &quot;Gangrel Methuselah ate packs of Get unchallenged&quot;. Fluff background text is usually BS. That's probably just me though. /shrug<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136982#post1136982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If one creature can alone achive the things which another must do together... yep, the first is more &quot;developed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? How so? I think maybe you are trying too hard to compare things. The different game lines operate on entirely different premises. For whatever reason, it would seem (to me) that you think cooperation = weakness. Which I certainly disagree with. Mind you, I think the eldest Vampires are in a power bracket beyond Fera (generally speaking). But that doesn't really matter because they were never meant to be taken down single handedly. Not even within their own setting. Vampire Methuselahs aren't meant to be defeated by a single PC. No matter what game line you're playing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1136982#post1136982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OK, after all - many people like Sabbat. Ang Garou still can - and do - kill, torture and humiliate others with impunity.<br /> Kill or be killed))</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They don't. Garou in general do not torture or humiliate. Torture is certainly &quot;of the Wyrm&quot;. Humiliation doesn't really come up much (in my experience). It can happen, but that is never an end in and of itself. On killing...yea that happens. But Garou don't (or shouldn't) kill indiscriminately or for fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-03-2017, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T22:54:38-07:00","id":1137198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137131#post1137131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Methuselahs aren't meant to be defeated by a single PC. No matter what game line you're playing.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Even for Achmage or Rank 6 Elder? If so, hence vampires is the most perfect kind in Wod.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T05:13:07-07:00","id":1137264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137131#post1137131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I treat most of those sorts of stories the same way I treat the &quot;Gangrel Methuselah ate packs of Get unchallenged&quot;. Fluff background text is usually BS. That's probably just me though. /shrug</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There is another parameter that has to be aadded in this matter, what player characters can achieve.<br /> Do you believe me that I had to split my player's pack in order not to <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\">blast</span> the campaign ?<br /> Wh<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">en they did unite they killed a nictuku ... and without much effort, it just happened by luck.<br /> Immagine what an elder like the Margrave can do.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137131#post1137131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Methuselahs aren't meant to be defeated by a single PC.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I completely agree with that, real life campaigns have another opinion though .... </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137131#post1137131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. They don't. Garou in general do not torture or humiliate. But Garou don't (or shouldn't) kill indiscriminately or for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such tactics are used from the garou in the form of dogpile pack tactic and Ragabashes tauntings, the no-moons really like to drive full mons crazy from time to time ....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T10:01:21-07:00","id":1137348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137198#post1137198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for Achmage or Rank 6 Elder? If so, hence vampires is the most perfect kind in Wod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't PCs. I really don't get your argument. There is no &quot;perfect&quot; supernatural in the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T10:56:18-07:00","id":1137365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137348#post1137348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no &quot;perfect&quot; supernatural in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a 100% accurate, the missunderstanding that a supernatural has the answer to all problems and can defeat all the others comes from simplification of rules, meta-game thinking and favouritism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T11:29:44-07:00","id":1137375,"title":"","content":"Just got time to respond from my computer (from my phone is harder to do)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137264#post1137264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is another parameter that has to be aadded in this matter, what player characters can achieve.<br /> Do you believe me that I had to split my player's pack in order not to the campaign ?<br /> When they did unite they killed a nictuku ... and without much effort, it just happened by luck.<br /> Immagine what an elder like the Margrave can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players always break the system. Point taken though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137264#post1137264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I completely agree with that, real life campaigns have another opinion though ....</div> </div> </div> </div>True. That's players for you though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137264#post1137264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Such tactics are used from the garou in the form of dogpile pack tactic and Ragabashes tauntings, the no-moons really like to drive full mons crazy from time to time ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Humiliation was less so than the other 2 examples (torture and random killing). But even with that, the point of the taunting isn't to humiliate. It's (in my experience) generally used as a distraction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T13:34:09-07:00","id":1137431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137375#post1137375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got time to respond from my computer (from my phone is harder to do)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Take your time friend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137375#post1137375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humiliation was less so than the other 2 examples (torture and random killing). But even with that, the point of the taunting isn't to humiliate. It's (in my experience) generally used as a distraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Torturing a wyrm creature is very likely to happen in a bad way...<br /> <br /> I agree though that the reason of an action, may or may not be reason for wyrm taint, which is way different from being evil, even though wyrm and evil go hand in hand in a plenty of cases.<br /> Sometimes even when you are mean with wyrm creatures like torturing a sentient fomor for fun, you may become wyrm tainted. while other times evil acts may not be wyrm tainted at all, like killing fire fighters who try to save innocents, because you want to save a fire elemental from their fire hoses. The act is evil but not wyrm tainted, though such cases are quite sensitive and its up to the story teller and the players on what game they want to play and with what situations they feel comfortable to deal with. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T14:42:11-07:00","id":1137453,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have never played in a game where the Garou considered torturing Wyrm creatures. For fun or not. Interrogation is generally different. And certainly never for fun. Torture for fun is a Wyrm-ish act imo.<br /> <br /> On the firefighter thing: that's not how the universe works (again, imo). Firefighters can't harm an elemental, because the fire spirit would be on the other side of the Gauntlet. Sure, the spirit might be annoyed at them for attacking its material correspondence, but they can't actually harm it (barring awakened water or fire hoses or some such weirdness). If the material fire needed to burn for some story reason, the Garou would be much better served impeding the firefighters efforts. Not killing them. And again, certainly not for fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T03:30:03-07:00","id":1137634,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately the elemental was summoned with a gift in the material side and the garou fed it with wood and other delicacies in order to pay chiminage and thank it for the aid it provided, that made a chain reaction of events that ended up with dead fire fighters. Anyway it was a huge plot.<br /> No it was not for fun it was serious scenario with dramatic scenes.<br /> <br /> In my campaigns there is core the theme that garou are monsters, capable of horrible things and indeed the player characters made many monstrous actions in a wonderful way. Were is in its core a horror game afterall, though in order to play horror scenes ypu must have mature players that like this kind of mood. <br /> <br /> For example. the philodox captured a female sergeant who marched with tanks and other kind of vehicles towards a kinfolk settlement, the pack destroyed the entire battalion and captures the superior alive. After an interogation (without torture) the philodox asked the woman ''do you understand the impact of your actions ?'' the woman replied &quot;I understand, I am sorry for causing trouble to so many families, I couln't have known'', the philodox replied ''good'' and then took her head off with his grand klaive. <br /> <br /> I got shocked! I asked him why he did that? and the player replied that through her ignorance and given her army rank, she was still posed a danger to the kinfolk and gaia.<br /> It didn't happen for fun, and the philodox's opinion actually had impact, though he could take the chance to gain a new ally, he chose punishment. But still I didn't expect such a reaction after a good social interaction that went totally to the way the philodox wanted. <br /> <br /> On another scene the pack took hispo an played with a fomori ..... with the bad meaning of playing, like wolves play with freshly killed prey, but with the fomori still alive, the players were laughing like crazy while screaming ''get a pass'' and I was in the middle of the table pulling off my hair <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T03:48:12-07:00","id":1137639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137634#post1137634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another scene the pack took hispo an played with a fomori ..... with the bad meaning of playing, like wolves play with freshly killed prey, but with the fomori still alive, the players were laughing like crazy while screaming ''get a pass'' and I was in the middle of the table pulling off my hair <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no, i mean the litany technically doesnt forbids that but any higher ranking Garou with an ounce of humanity would probably intervene by order them to stop and just kill the poor thing. And follow that by a &quot;What the shit guys?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-05-2017, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:03:18-07:00","id":1137731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137639#post1137639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah no, i mean the litany technically doesnt forbids that but any higher ranking Garou with an ounce of humanity would probably intervene by order them to stop and just kill the poor thing. And follow that by a &quot;What the shit guys?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think garou do torture for the sake of torture at parts. But it is the same way as with people, someone is a jackass and gets an ego boost over beating those weaker than them. Some Shadow Lord abuse their kinfolk. Fianna, Fangs and Wendigo have an unspoken permission to treat their metis roughly. But I think you need to -actually- be the kind of person who would do it to actually do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:38:24-07:00","id":1137752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1133131-why-do-you-like-wta?p=1137731#post1137731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think garou do torture for the sake of torture at parts. But it is the same way as with people, someone is a jackass and gets an ego boost over beating those weaker than them. Some Shadow Lord abuse their kinfolk. Fianna, Fangs and Wendigo have an unspoken permission to treat their metis roughly. But I think you need to -actually- be the kind of person who would do it to actually do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely with you apart from the <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ''b<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">e kind of person who would do it to actually do it''</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> thing, other thing is the in-game role playing and other thing is the real person behind the character, me m